# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
[Pp]ublish/
*.nupkg

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDEs - Visual Studio, Rider. (.vscode/ is tracked on purpose: launch/tasks)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.pubxml.user

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests and logs
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.trx
coverage*/
*.coverage
*.log
[Ll]ogs/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets - never commit keys, certificates or local overrides
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Face recognition models (~255MB). Downloaded by scripts/download-models.ps1
# into src/Api/models/. "**/" is required: a pattern containing a slash is
# otherwise anchored to the repo root and would miss src/Api/models/. GitHub
# rejects files over 100MB, so a missed model breaks the push.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/models/*.onnx

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Face photos and biometric data - must never be committed.
# Anchored on purpose: a bare "storage/" also matched the source folder
# src/Infra/Storage/, because git on Windows ignores case, and silently kept
# the image-store code out of the repo.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/storage/
/src/Api/storage/
# Ad-hoc test photos dropped next to the scripts.
/scripts/*.png
/scripts/*.jpg
/scripts/*.jpeg
# The synthetic placeholders in docs/samples are tracked deliberately;
# real photos go under a personal/ subfolder, which is not.
docs/samples/personal/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local databases
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS clutter
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
